#: ../../source/model-zoo/models/hdhkt.md:15 d7e7a104274b40beb060c1239c91cce8
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Accurate knowledge tracing (KT) for predicting students’ future "
"performance is critical for personalized learning and intelligent "
"educational systems. Recent approaches extend sequential modeling with "
"graph structures to capture structural dependencies in learning "
"processes, yielding promising results. However, existing methods still "
"suffer from insufficient modeling of heterogeneous educational entities "
"and relations as well as limited capacity for higher-order structure "
"modeling. To address these challenges, we propose Heterogeneous graph and"
" Difficulty-aware Hypergraph fusion for Knowledge Tracing (HDHKT). "
"Specifically, we construct a heterogeneous graph to model diverse "
"relations among questions, concepts, and auxiliary entities, including "
"templates and assignments. To capture higher-order structures, we "
"introduce a difficulty-aware weighted hypergraph over questions. "
"Furthermore, we design a Mixture-of-Experts (MoE)-based dynamic fusion "
"mechanism to adaptively integrate representations from different "
"structural views. Experiments on ASSISTments 2009, ASSISTments 2012, and "
"EdNet show that HDHKT achieves state-of-the-art performance, with AUC "
"improvements of up to 2.75% and ACC gains of up to 1.76% over strong "
"baselines, while maintaining competitive performance across datasets. "
"Ablation studies examine the contribution of each component, and "
"qualitative analyses further demonstrate its interpretability and "
"effectiveness in tracking knowledge state dynamics. The code for HDHKT is"
" available at https://github.com/szhhwh/HDHKT."
msgstr ""
"Accurate knowledge tracing (KT) for predicting students’ future "
"performance is critical for personalized learning and intelligent "
"educational systems. Recent approaches extend sequential modeling with "
"graph structures to capture structural dependencies in learning "
"processes, yielding promising results. However, existing methods still "
"suffer from insufficient modeling of heterogeneous educational entities "
"and relations as well as limited capacity for higher-order structure "
"modeling. To address these challenges, we propose Heterogeneous graph and"
" Difficulty-aware Hypergraph fusion for Knowledge Tracing (HDHKT). "
"Specifically, we construct a heterogeneous graph to model diverse "
"relations among questions, concepts, and auxiliary entities, including "
"templates and assignments. To capture higher-order structures, we "
"introduce a difficulty-aware weighted hypergraph over questions. "
"Furthermore, we design a Mixture-of-Experts (MoE)-based dynamic fusion "
"mechanism to adaptively integrate representations from different "
"structural views. Experiments on ASSISTments 2009, ASSISTments 2012, and "
"EdNet show that HDHKT achieves state-of-the-art performance, with AUC "
"improvements of up to 2.75% and ACC gains of up to 1.76% over strong "
"baselines, while maintaining competitive performance across datasets. "
"Ablation studies examine the contribution of each component, and "
"qualitative analyses further demonstrate its interpretability and "
"effectiveness in tracking knowledge state dynamics. The code for HDHKT is"
" available at https://github.com/szhhwh/HDHKT."

